;
; How Moraine files an escrow's guardian hierarchy, in MYRA
; (moraine_rules.h MR4): under the escrow, each guardian (1 .. 5, zxvd's
; index plus one) with the guardian above it (parent, 0 for the owner at
; the top), its rank (1 just under the owner) and when it was added, in
; seconds since 1970. Never a key's bytes: there is no field for one. The
; model asks whether the numbers fit, and checks the tree itself (no
; guardian under itself or under one of its own), before it keeps one.
^ZXMORAINE(escrow:i9, guardian:i1) = parent:i1! ^ rank:i1! ^ added:i12!
